  "conclusion": "hipEngine already exceeds llama.cpp HIP decode at all six shapes, but needs 16.3-87.0% prefill uplift to match HIP, 5.9-20.1% decode uplift to match Vulkan, and a 1.31-1.40 GiB tracked-memory reduction at 4K-128K to reach the HIP whole-device rows. Exact GDN dominates prefill. Bulk-prefill scratch is 1.75-1.76 GiB at 4K+, large enough to close the HIP memory gap if its liveness is reduced to about 0.35-0.45 GiB. Current 4K decode is 39.3% dense Q8 T16 GEMV and 20.3% selected-MoE GEMV; launch count is already only about 708 kernels/token.",
